@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### Create an order (the response never depends on RabbitMQ)
# @name createOrder
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: demo-{{$randomInt}}

{
  "customerId": "customer-42",
  "items": [
    { "sku": "SKU-1", "quantity": 2, "unitPrice": 149.90 },
    { "sku": "SKU-2", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 59.90 }
  ]
}

### Read it back
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{createOrder.response.body.$.orderId}}

### Order that inventory rejects (SKU-5 is seeded with zero stock): a business outcome, not an error
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "customer-42",
  "items": [ { "sku": "SKU-5", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 39.90 } ]
}

### Order whose consumer always fails (docker-compose sets Inventory__FailOnSku=SKU-FAIL): retries, then DLQ
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "customer-42",
  "items": [ { "sku": "SKU-FAIL", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 1.00 } ]
}

### Invalid order -> 400 problem details, nothing written to the outbox
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "",
  "items": []
}

### Outbox state (pending / processed / failed)
GET {{baseUrl}}/diagnostics/outbox

### Health: Postgres decides readiness; RabbitMQ down only shows as Degraded
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/ready
